## What to deliver

Build and rig the hatchery up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a squat, wide hive-mound clustered with amber-glowing
hatch cells (the fixed body), a central iris hatch on the crown, and a vent set into the
side. **Author the two required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation
subcommands: `hatch_turn` (the hatch sweeping smoothly through a full turn about its
vertical axis, eased so it carries weight rather than sliding linearly) and `vent_bob`
(the vent lifting off its seat and settling back with weight). The animations are the
fixed contract — produce both, by those names, both self-playing and looping; the parts
and joints that realize them are yours. Before you finish, run `voxel-anim render` so it
emits the per-part `.glb` geometry your result is built from — an unrendered part is
scored as empty (`voxel-anim render --component <part>` redraws one part; `voxel-anim
render --time <ms> --animation <name>` renders the model posed at that instant of an
animation to check the motion). When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs
and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
